  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 208 AM MDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nDry cold front will move through the area today. We should see \ncooler temps today with highs in the 80s to around 90. Breezy \nconditions are likely today. The INL/Craters area may touch wind\nadvisory levels but everywhere else should remain under those \nthresholds. HRRR smoke models shows a burst of smoke moving into\neast Idaho this morning. But the smoke should dissipate around \nmid afternoon with the breezy conditions. Some hazy skies could \nlinger into Monday. The upper level flow turns northwesterly \nbehind the front which will allow for noticeably cooler temps \nfor Monday into Tuesday with highs in the upper 70s to mid 80s. \nHowever the ridge will reestablish itself for mid to late week. \nWeather looks continued dry at this point.",
